abstract: >-
  A versioned research infrastructure for studying immigrant-serving journalism
  across the United States. Version 1.0 (Phase 1A) is a frozen national baseline:
  531 assessed records and 301 core verified outlets or journalism products
  across all 50 states and the District of Columbia, with codebooks, data
  dictionary, review decisions, audit summaries, build scripts, and SHA-256
  checksums. The map serves as a sampling frame, not a census, for later
  institutional enrichment, risk-event coding, and interview research on how
  organizational capacity shapes exposure to legal, physical, political,
  economic, and informational risk.
